<p>Set the image quality and color tone.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="profile" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile:</span></p>
<p>Select a color profile pattern.</p>
<p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">By Each Component</span>, different 
 settings can be assigned to each element of text, photographic, and presentation.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, the available items may vary.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_COLORPROFILE">Changing the Color Profiling Pattern</a></p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Automatically configures the best color profile 
 pattern depending on the appearance of the document to print.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic (Brighter)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Automatically configures the best color profile pattern to be brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic (Darker)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Automatically configures the best color profile pattern to be darker.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Optimizes the colors for text.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text (Brighter)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Optimizes the colors for text to be brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text (Darker)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Optimizes the colors for text to be darker.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances mid-tone colors similar to those seen in 
 photographs.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic (Brighter)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances mid-tone colors, similar to those seen in photographs, to be 
 brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic (Darker)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances mid-tone colors, similar to those seen in photographs, to be 
 darker.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Presentation</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics. 
 This setting is best for printing tables, graphs, and presentation materials 
 that contain color.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Presentation (Brighter)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics 
 to be brighter.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Presentation (Darker)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics 
 to be darker.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">CAD</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances reproduction of even colors that are true 
 to the original.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">POP Display</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the color red more vividly. It is an optimal 
 setting for the POP display.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 1 (Bright/Yellow)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances colors suitable for portraits.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 2 (Dark/Red)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances colors suitable for portraits or food.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 3 (Darker/Blue)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints the color blue more vividly. Suitable for 
 landscapes.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 4 (Dark/Yellow)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances dark-tone colors over the whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 5 (Brighter/Red)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances bright-tone colors over the whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 6 (Brighter/Yellow)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances brightness and contrast over the whole 
 area.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Variation 7 (Darker/Red)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances dark-tone colors and contrast over the 
 whole area.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Off</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints colors without modification.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Use ICM</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Corrects colors using the Windows ICM function.</p>
<p class="Normal-indent"><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_ICM">Using ICM</a></p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Expand Gray Recognition</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Checks every pixel and prints gray pixels (when 
 the values of RGB are equal or nearly equal) using black toner only.<br/>
This setting is available only if you have selected <span class="Term-Soft">K: 
 Expand Gray Recognition</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Gray Reproduction:</span> 
 list.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free Color Management</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Converts the colors used in documents to the barrier-free 
 colors applicable to Color Universal Design (CUD).</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">This setting is available only if you have selected 
 <span class="Term-Soft">On</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Barrier-free 
 Color Management:</span> list.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="dither" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Dithering:</span></p>
<p>Select a dithering pattern suitable for the document image.</p>
<p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">By Each Component</span>, different 
 settings can be assigned to each element of text, photographic, and presentation.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, the available items may vary.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_DITHERING">Changing the Dithering Pattern</a></p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Automatic</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Automatically configures the best dithering method 
 depending on the appearance of the document to print.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Photographic</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Performs dithering using a pattern appropriate for 
 photographs.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Text</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Performs dithering using a pattern appropriate for 
 text.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Thin lines</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Performs dithering using a pattern appropriate for 
 thin lines. Thin colored lines can be seen easily.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">CAD</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Performs dithering using a pattern appropriate for 
 CAD printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="gray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Gray Reproduction:</span></p>
<p>Select the printing method appropriate for black and gray areas of documents.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">K (Black)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints black and gray using black toner only. Compared 
 to the black printed with CMYK toner, this results in a black that is 
 relatively flatter and purer.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Depending on 
 the application you are using, black and gray images may print with CMYK 
 toner even if <span class="Term-Soft">K (Black)</span> is selected.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">CMY + K</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints black and gray on all pages using four colors: 
 CMY (Cyan, Magenta, and Yellow) and K (Black).</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">K(Black) for Text</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints black and gray text using black toner only.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">K (Black) for Gray Pixels Only</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Checks every pixel and prints gray pixels (when 
 the values of RGB are equal) using black toner only. Other pixels are 
 printed using CMYK toner.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">K: Expand Gray Recognition</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Checks every pixel and prints gray pixels (when 
 the values of RGB are equal or nearly equal) using black toner only.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent"><span class="Term-Soft">Color 
 Balance</span> is set to <span class="Term-Soft">Expand Gray Recognition</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Black/Gray by K-Strong UCR</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Prints all black and gray objects using black toner 
 only regardless of whether the document is in color or black and white.<br/>
This is useful when a black and gray image or scanned black text might 
 print with CMYK toner even if <span class="Term-Soft">K (Black)</span> is 
 selected.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="colormethod" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Color Profile Method:</span></p>
<p>Specify how to print your color graphics.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">By Host System</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">A color management system (ICM) function or color 
 matching is performed by the host computer before the document is sent 
 to the printer.</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">ICM is performed by the OS, and color matching by 
 the printer driver.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">By Printer</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Color matching is performed by the printer.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">By Printer Driver</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">ICM is performed by the printer driver.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="intent" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">ICM Intent:</span></p>
<p>Specify how color images are created to produce the best looking image 
 on the printed page.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function is available only if <span class="Term-Soft">By 
 Printer Driver</span> is already selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">Color 
 Profile Method:</span> list.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Graphics (Saturation)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances basic colors used for text and graphics. 
 This setting is best for printing tables, graphs, and presentation materials 
 that contain color.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Pictures (Perceptual)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Enhances mid-tone colors similar to those seen in 
 photographs.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Proof (Relative Colorimetric)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Renders colors in an image with the closest colors 
 possible. This is suitable for printing colors that need to be rendered 
 accurately, such as colors in logos. The colors that fall outside the 
 printer color gamut will be rendered to the closest color possible.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Match (Absolute Colorimetric)</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Assuming a device-independent color space, this 
 provides a wider range of colors than the printer color gamut.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this tab to the default settings.</p>
